 "eco_finding": "post-route hold ECO = repair_timing -hold on RCX parasitics + re-route. Incremental GRT over kept detailed wires breaks DRT (~1M violations); keeping the clock wires fails DRT connectivity; a full signal+clock re-route works (DRC 0) but moves setup by -1 (hc) to -24 ps (sfu) and skew-dependent hold by up to -27 ps. HC (SS +70) absorbs it and closes; light (+41) and sfu (+52) cannot: both are limited by the gather index path (q_sh -> vi_q << sh + a -> rd_addr_r, one cycle) and light also by the imm3 compare into p_a (b_q cx_imm3 -> okey -> kge -> pre_a2 -> p_a). Owner rule: change the RTL (gather shift register +1 cycle on gathers, imm3 key precompute) in the shared SU c12 lane / controller depth model, then one route each.",
